## Lore

The officers of CAF Fleet Command are trained in leadership and in a spread of
technical specialties, because the Consortium operates across galactic distances
and an officer is routinely a long way from the command structure that would
otherwise tell him what to do. Initiative is the selection criterion: those who
hesitate are shunted to rear-echelon console jobs in the less elite CAF Officers
Corps, who are run as ordinary CAF Troopers.

The ones who graduate come out able to command a starship, fight it ship to
ship, survive in the wilderness and conduct guerrilla warfare with improvised
weapons. Many end up as secret agents or in elite Special Forces units.

Against Transgalactic Empire officers, who follow orders more closely and drill
to a stricter standard, the CAF officer''s self-reliance is an edge - though in
large-scale battles the Empire sometimes has the better of it, because CAF
officers tend to lose the big picture.

## Pay and posting

Money is 3D6x100 credits. Cybernetics are none to start with; most
civilizations of the Three Galaxies avoid them.

## GM Notes

No amount of training predicts how a Fleet Officer handles a real situation,
which the book says outright. Overall they are among the most resourceful beings
in the Three Galaxies, and the class is written to be played that way rather
than as a rank.
